addition+='There is substantial actual sharing too. Inference borrows the Distillery-held model library; deferred composition waits for the personal graph, and ordered close ends inference before Distillery. Private inference uses the existing group/keyring through a live protection handle, retaining address/domain and writer checks rather than creating another group engine. Discovery binds signed endpoint hints to the carrier, graph and current reader. Automatic settings cap candidate count, tensor frames and time bounds, including the mesh lease ceiling. The Chronicle consumes authoritative folded boards beside lifecycle receipts; it is not an independent fold. CPU/GPU fixtures share resident setup while explicitly acknowledging duplicated synthetic weight construction in another package. No GPU/trainer run is claimed from reading those tests.\n\n'
addition+='Two suspicions were ruled out through source tracing: dynamic MeshHost::register_resource advances facts.gpu when a GPU stage is registered, despite older trainer-only comments; and GraphSession first-edit forks clone their parent validator, preventing the suspected loss of domain validation in the read-only-thaw path. The current resident-mere production prefix also checks live route grants and avoids minting a session for ambient open. That file is still partial, and its original tests are not counted as read or executed. Multi-catalog registration failure and live sync-disable semantics remain qualified candidates, not new proven failures.\n\n'
addition+='Fresh checks: four no-inference unit tests pass, proving the default build refuses configured inference and retains strict model schemas. Seven stage-enabled unit tests pass, covering model/limit/build gates, attestation codec and signed discovery facts. Three public native observations pass: two settings interleavings and one in-memory selector/replica composition. The settings observations use actual pair_device/unpair_device and OwnerSettings APIs with synthetic profile files; no timed resident process race or live cryptographic re-admission was run. The selector observation uses the exact host builder chain with public replicas; no full host or network was opened. Preliminary probe failures came from a Windows CRLF marker assumption and treating correct local NotSelected refusal as setup success; those failed sources/logs have a separate preserved receipt. The corrected probe uses legacy node projection and checks refusal as its control. Product source was untouched.\n\n'
